+          description: >-
+            The address of this node's content. It MAY name a model, or the Spatial, Node or wow/world
+            resource of any world, which is then shown at this node. A client MUST tell them apart by the
+            media type of the answer, never by the address or the content: application/wow+json marks a Web
+            of Worlds resource. The including node stands in for the included node's parent. A whole world
+            shows its default graph, and its other anchored graphs where their GeoPoses put them. The
+            included world's environment MUST NOT apply to the host. The host MUST set a nesting limit and a
+            budget of included graphs, which it hands out in tree order (depth first, children in order). It
+            MUST refuse an inclusion that closes a cycle, detected by URL, and SHOULD show a placeholder on failure.
+            A host MUST read an included part from the part's own world, at its URL, and MUST revalidate it by
+            its entity tag. A copy of that part relayed or embedded by any other world MUST NOT be shown as that
+            part. When the part's own world does not answer, the host SHOULD show the placeholder.
